对于情况 3，其实是#strong[计算模式的根本性不一致]。我们再次关注注意力计算的核心：`attn_scores = query @ key.T`。

- #strong[请求A (Initiation Phase)]:
  - #strong[目标]: 计算输入的 `L_A` 个词元#strong[内部]两两之间的关系。
  - #strong[计算模式]: `query` 长度 `L_q` 是 `L_A`，`key` 长度 `L_k` 也是 `L_A`。需要计算一个 `L_A x L_A` 的注意力矩阵。
- #strong[请求B (Increment Phase)]:
  - #strong[目标]: 计算#strong[1个]新词元与过去 `L_B` 个历史词元的关系。
  - #strong[计算模式]: `query` 长度 `L_q` 是 #strong[1]，`key` 长度 `L_k` 是 `L_B`。需要计算一个 `1 x L_B` 的注意力向量。

#strong[这里的核心冲突是 `query` 的长度 `L_q` 不同。]

- 请求A有 `L_A` 个“提问者”（queries）。
- 请求B只有 `1` 个“提问者”（query）。

你无法通过 Padding 来统一 `query` 的数量。给请求B补齐 `query` 是没有意义的，因为它只有一个“思考焦点”。一个批次的矩阵乘法无法做到：对批次中的第一个元素计算一个 `L_A x L_A` 的结果，同时对第二个元素计算一个 `1 x L_B` 的结果。

== Solution 2: Selective Batching
Instead of processing a batch of requests by “batchifying” all tensor operations composing the model, this technique selectively apply batching only to a handful of operations.

#img("/assets/images/pasted-image-20250702143330.png", alt: "pasted-image-20250702143330")
Core insight:

- Operations such as non-Attention matrix multiplication and layer normalization can be made to work with irregularly shaped tensors by flattening the tensors.
- The Attention operation requires a notion of requests (i.e., requires the batch dimension) to compute attention only between the tokens of the same request, typically done by applying cuBLAS routines for batch matrix multiplication.

Selective batching: #strong[it splits the batch and processes each request individually for the Attention operation while applying token-wise (instead of request-wise) batching to other operations without the notion of requests.]

#quote(block: true)[
To make the requests in the increment phase can use the Attention keys and values for the tokens processed in previous iterations, ORCA maintains the generated keys and values in the Attention K/V manager.
]

= Design
== Distributed Architecture
为了支持单 GPU 无法容纳的大模型，ORCA 的执行引擎采用了两种成熟的并行化技术 ：

- #strong[层内并行 (Intra-layer parallelism)]: 将模型单层内的矩阵乘法（如 `Linear` 和 `Attention` 操作）及其参数切分到多个GPU上执行 。
- #strong[层间并行 (Inter-layer parallelism)]: 将模型的不同 Transformer 层垂直切分到不同的GPU组（即 Workers）上，形成流水线 。

#img("/assets/images/pasted-image-20250702143619.png", alt: "pasted-image-20250702143619")
#img("/assets/images/pasted-image-20250702143632.png", alt: "pasted-image-20250702143632")
#strong[Components:]

- #strong[Engine Master:]~Receives commands from a scheduler and forwards batch info to the first pipeline stage (Worker).
- #strong[Worker:]~Each worker manages a model partition (a pipeline stage) across multiple GPUs.
- #strong[Controller:]~An internal component of a Worker that dispatches tasks to its GPUs and forwards control messages.

#strong[Execution Flow:]

+ #strong[Initiation:]~The Engine Master sends batch info (tokens & metadata) to the first worker (Worker 1).
+ #strong[Pipelined Forwarding:]~Worker 1\'s Controller dispatches tasks to its local GPUs and~immediately~forwards the control message to the next worker (Worker 2) without waiting for its local computation to complete.
+ #strong[Synchronization Point:]~Only the~last~worker in the pipeline waits for its GPU computations to finish before returning the output tokens to the Engine Master.

#strong[Key Optimization: Control-Data Plane Separation]

- #strong[Problem:]~Traditional systems (e.g., Faster Transformer) use NCCL for all communication, including small control messages, causing unnecessary CPU-GPU synchronization overhead.
- #strong[ORCA\'s Solution:]
  - #strong[Control Plane:]~Small control messages (metadata) are sent via standard CPU-based networking (e.g., gRPC).
  - #strong[Data Plane:]~Large intermediate tensors (activations) are transferred between GPUs using NCCL.
- #strong[Benefit:]~This separation minimizes sync overhead and improves distributed efficiency.

== Scheduling Algorithm
The scheduler re-evaluates batches every iteration based on these principles:

- #strong[Fairness (Iteration-Level FCFS):]~Prioritizes requests that arrived earlier. If request~A~arrived before~B,~A\'s executed iteration count will always be ≥~B\'s.
- #strong[Throughput/Latency Trade-off (max\_batch\_size):]~Uses a configurable~max\_bs~to maximize throughput within a given latency budget.
- #strong[KV Cache-Aware Memory Management:]
  - #strong[Constraint:]~Limited GPU memory for the KV cache is a key bottleneck.
  - #strong[Solution:]~To prevent deadlocks, the scheduler pre-allocates the full KV cache space a new request might need (based on its~max\_tokens) before scheduling it. A request is only added if this reservation succeeds.

#img("/assets/images/pasted-image-20250702144338.png", alt: "pasted-image-20250702144338")
- #strong[Pipeline Parallelism (Keeping the Pipeline Full):]
  - #strong[Mechanism:]~The scheduler keeps injecting batches until the number of in-flight batches equals the number of workers (n\_scheduled = n\_workers).
  - #strong[Benefit:]~This ensures all workers are always busy, eliminating pipeline \"bubbles\" (idle stages) and maximizing hardware utilization.
  - #strong[Advantage:]~More efficient than Faster Transformer\'s microbatching, as it avoids the trade-off between batch efficiency and pipeline efficiency.
